.TH CALC 1 "2026-06-09" "1.1.1" "eggcalc Manual"
.ad l
.nh

.SH NAME
calc \- natural language math expression calculator

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcalc\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIEXPRESSION\fR]
.PP
\fBcalc\fR \fB\-i\fR
.PP
\fBecho\fR \e"5 + 3\e" | \fBcalc\fR \fB\-e\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBcalc\fR is a command-line calculator that accepts natural language expressions and converts them into mathematical operations. It supports unit conversions, scientific functions, physical constants, complex numbers, and more.
.PP
Unlike traditional calculators, \fBcalc\fR understands plain English:
.PP
.nf
  $ calc \e"five plus three\e"
  8
  $ calc \e"30 meters plus 100 feet\e"
  60.48 m
  $ calc \e"sin of pi over two\e"
  1.0
.fi

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB--help\fR
Show help message with all available operators, units, constants, and examples.

.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB--version\fR
Show version information and exit.

.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB--expression\fR \fIEXPRESSION\fR
Evaluate a single expression. By default, outputs only the result (quiet mode). This is the recommended mode for piping input.

.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB--quiet\fR
Suppress the expression in output, showing only the numeric result.

.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB--show\fR
Accepted for compatibility. Plain output remains result-only.

.TP
\fB--json\fR
Output result as JSON with \fBresult\fR and \fBexpression\fR fields:
.PP
.nf
  $ calc --json \e"5 + 3\e"
  {"result": 8, "expression": "5+3"}
.fi

.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB--interactive\fR
Start interactive REPL mode. Enter expressions directly, type \fBquit\fR or \fBexit\fR to exit:
.PP
.nf
  $ calc -i
  >>> five plus three
  8
  >>> sqrt(144)
  12.0
  >>> 30m + 100ft
  60.48 m
  >>> quit
.fi

.TP
\fB--mcp\fR
Run as an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server for AI agent integration. The server exposes text and math tools via JSON-RPC over stdin/stdout. See the \fBMCP SERVER MODE\fR section for details.

.SH ARGUMENTS

.TP
\fIEXPRESSION\fR
The math expression to evaluate. Can include:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Arithmetic: \fB+\fR, \fB-\fR, \fB*\fR, \fB/\fR, \fB**\fR (power), \fB%\fR (modulo)
.IP \(bu
Number words: \fBzero\fR, \fBone\fR, \fBtwo\fR, ..., \fBmillion\fR, \fBbillion\fR
.IP \(bu
Natural language operators: \fBplus\fR, \fBminus\fR, \fBtimes\fR, \fBdivided by\fR
.IP \(bu
Functions: \fBsin\fR, \fBcos\fR, \fBsqrt\fR, \fBlog\fR, \fBabs\fR, etc.
.IP \(bu
Units: \fBm\fR, \fBft\fR, \fBkg\fR, \fBgal\fR, etc.
.IP \(bu
Constants: \fBpi\fR, \fBe\fR, \fBavogadro\fR, \fBplanck\fR, etc.
.RE

.SH TEXT INSPECTION TOOLS

\fBcalc\fR includes text inspection tools for detecting hidden characters, testing patterns, and analyzing text security risks.

.SS inspect - Hidden Character Detection

Check text for invisible characters and confusables:
.PP
.nf
  $ calc inspect \e"hello\e"
  \(bu No hidden characters

  $ calc inspect \e"user\x00name\e"
  \(bu HIDDEN: Text contains NULL (U+0000) at index 5.

  $ calc inspect \e"p$'\u0430'ypal\e"   # Cyrillic 'а' looks like Latin 'a'
  \(bu CONFUSABLE: Text contains confusable character '\(e2' (looks like 'a') at index 1.
.fi
.PP
This uses the Unicode UTS #39 confusables database (6500+ entries) to detect homoglyph attacks.

.SS count - Character Counting

Count character occurrences with optional frequency table:
.PP
.nf
  $ calc count \e"hello\e" l
  'l' appears 3 time(s) in \e"hello\e"

  $ calc count \e"hello world"\e"
  \e"hello world\e":
    11 characters
    'l': 3
    'o': 2
    'e': 1
    (space): 1
    'h': 1
    'w': 1
    'r': 1
    'd': 1
.fi

.SS regex - Pattern Testing

Test regex patterns against sample text:
.PP
.nf
  $ calc regex \e"^\ed+$\e" \e"12345\e"
  \(bu Match: '12345'

  $ calc regex \e"(\ed+)-(\ed+)\e" \e"555-1234\e"
  \(bu Match: '555-1234'
    Groups: ('555', '1234')
.fi

.SH MCP SERVER MODE

When run with \fB--mcp\fR, \fBcalc\fR acts as a Model Context Protocol server exposing exact text and math tools to AI agents. This enables AI agents to perform deterministic text analysis and math calculations.

.SS Available Tools

.TP
\fBmath_eval\fR
Evaluate math expressions with full natural language and unit support.
.TP
\fBtext_measure\fR
Return text metrics: UTF-8 bytes, codepoint count, word count, line count, whitespace analysis, newline style, Unicode normalization state.
.TP
\fBtext_equal\fR
Compare strings with normalization options (raw, NFC, NFD, NFKC, NFKD, casefold, trim) and detailed evidence.
.TP
\fBtext_diff_explain\fR
Explain differences between strings with codepoint details, Unicode names, normalization differences, and security findings.
.TP
\fBtext_inspect\fR
Complete text inspection: hidden characters, Unicode confusables, mixed scripts, normalization state, and security warnings.
.TP
\fBtext_count\fR
Count character occurrences or return frequency table.
.TP
\fBvalidate_brackets\fR
Check bracket balance for \fB()\fR, \fB[]\fR, \fB{}\fR, \fB<>\fR with unmatched opener/closer details.
.TP
\fBvalidate_json\fR
Validate JSON and report parse errors with line, column, and position.
.TP
\fBvalidate_regex\fR
Test regex patterns against samples, report matches and capture groups.
.TP
\fBlist_compare\fR
Compare two lists with options for order sensitivity, casefold, and normalization.

.SS Protocol

The server uses JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdin/stdout:
.PP
.nf
  # List available tools
  {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": "tools/list"}

  # Call a tool
  {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "method": "tools/call",
   "params": {"name": "math_eval", "arguments": {"expression": "5 + 3"}}}
.fi

.SS Example Session

.PP
.nf
  $ calc --mcp
  {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": "tools/list"}
  # Response: {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"tools": [...]}}

  {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "method": "tools/call",
   "params": {"name": "math_eval", "arguments": {"expression": "2**10"}}}
  # Response: {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"ok": true, "result": 1024}}
.fi

.SH EXAMPLES

.SS Basic Arithmetic

.PP
.nf
  $ calc \e"2 + 2\e"
  4

  $ calc \e"10 / 3\e"
  3.3333333333333335

  $ calc \e"2 ** 10\e"
  1024
.fi

.SS Natural Language

.PP
.nf
  $ calc \e"five plus three\e"
  8

  $ calc \e"twenty times five\fR"
  100

  $ calc \e"what is the square root of one hundred\fR"
  10.0

  $ calc \e"one hundred fifty times three\fR"
  15000
.fi

.SS Order of Operations

\fBcalc\fR follows standard mathematical precedence:
.PP
.nf
  $ calc \e"five plus three times two\fR"
  11   # NOT 16 (multiplication before addition)

  $ calc \e"(five plus three) times two\fR"
  16  # Parentheses override precedence
.fi

.SS Unit Conversions

Use the \fBin\fR keyword to convert between units:
.PP
.nf
  $ calc \e"100ft in meters\fR"
  30.48 m

  $ calc \e"5km in miles\fR"
  3.107 mi

  $ calc \e"1GB in MB\fR"
  1024 MB
.fi

.SS Unit Arithmetic

Add, subtract, multiply units directly:
.PP
.nf
  $ calc \e"30m + 100ft\fR"
  60.48 m

  $ calc \e"2h + 30min\fR"
  2.5 h

  $ calc \e"60mi / h\fR"
  60 mi/h
.fi

.SS Temperature Conversions

Use the \fBtemp()\fR function for temperature:
.PP
.nf
  $ calc \e"temp(100, C, F)\fR"
  212.0

  $ calc \e"temp(32, F, C)\fR"
  0.0

  $ calc \e"temp(0, C, K)\fR"
  273.15
.fi

.SS Scientific Functions

.PP
.nf
  $ calc \e"sin(pi/2)\fR"
  1.0

  $ calc \e"sqrt(144)\fR"
  12.0

  $ calc \e"log(e)\fR"
  1.0

  $ calc \e"factorial(5)\fR"
  120

  $ calc \e"gcd(12, 18)\fR"
  6
.fi

.SS Complex Numbers

.PP
.nf
  $ calc \e"sqrt(-1)\fR"
  1j

  $ calc \e"3+4i\fR"
  (3+4j)

  $ calc \e"abs(3+4i)\fR"
  5.0

  $ calc \e"log(-1)\fR"
  3.141592653589793j
.fi

.SS Physical Constants

.PP
.nf
  $ calc \e"pi\fR"
  3.141592653589793

  $ calc \e"avogadro\fR"
  6.02214076e+23

  $ calc \e"speed of light\fR"
  299792458

  $ calc \e"5 * planck\fR"
  3.313e-33

  $ calc \e"h * c / 500nm\fR"  # Photon energy
  3.972e-19
.fi

.SS Pipe Input

.PP
.nf
  $ echo \e"5 + 3\fR" | calc -e
  8

  $ echo \e"100ft in meters\fR" | calc -e
  30.48
.fi

.SS Bitwise Operations

.PP
.nf
  $ calc \e"5 AND 3\fR"
  1

  $ calc \e"0xFF & 0x0F\fR"
  15

  $ calc \e"bin(255)\fR"
  '0xff'
.fi

.SH NATURAL LANGUAGE REFERENCE

.SS Number Words

.TP
Basic (0-9):
\fBzero\fR, \fBone\fR, \fBtwo\fR, \fBthree\fR, \fBfour\fR, \fBfive\fR, \fBsix\fR, \fBseven\fR, \fBeight\fR, \fBnine\fR

.TP
Teens (10-19):
\fBten\fR, \fBeleven\fR, \fBtwelve\fR, \fBthirteen\fR, \fBfourteen\fR, \fBfifteen\fR, \fBsixteen\fR, \fBseventeen\fR, \fBeighteen\fR, \fBnineteen\fR

.TP
Tens (20-90):
\fBtwenty\fR, \fBthirty\fR, \fBforty\fR, \fBfifty\fR, \fBsixty\fR, \fBseventy\fR, \fBeighty\fR, \fBninety\fR

.TP
Scales:
\fBhundred\fR, \fBthousand\fR, \fBmillion\fR, \fBbillion\fR, \fBtrillion\fR, \fBquadrillion\fR, \fBquintillion\fR

.TP
Fractions:
\fBhalf\fR, \fBquarter\fR, \fBthousandth\fR, \fBmillionth\fR, \fBbillionth\fR

.SS Number Combinations

Numbers combine according to these rules:
.PP
.nf
  # Ones + Tens: "twenty five" -> 25
  $ calc \e"twenty five\fR"
  25

  # Scale + Scale: "million billion" -> 1,000,000,000,000
  $ calc \e"million billion\fR"
  1e+15

  # "point" for decimals: "three point one four" -> 3.14
  $ calc \e"three point one four\fR"
  3.14
.fi

.SS Operator Words

.TP
\fBplus\fR, \fBpositive\fR -> \fB+\fR
.TP
\fBminus\fR, \fBnegative\fR -> \fB-\fR
.TP
\fBtimes\fR, \fBmultiplied by\fR, \fBof\fR -> \fB*\fR
.TP
\fBdivided by\fR, \fBover\fR, \fBper\fR, \fBdivide\fR -> \fB/\fR
.TP
\fBto the power of\fR, \fBraised to\fR -> \fB**\fR
.TP
\fBmod\fR, \fBmodulo\fR, \fBpercent\fR, \fBremainder\fR -> \fB%\fR

.SS Stripped Phrases

Certain conversational phrases are automatically removed:
.PP
.nf
  $ calc \e"what is five plus three\fR"
  8

  $ calc \e"calculate the square root of 16\fR"
  4.0

  $ calc \e"convert 100 meters to feet\fR"
  328.084 ft
.fi
.PP
Stripped phrases: \fBwhat's\fR, \fBwhat is\fR, \fBcalculate\fR, \fBcompute\fR, \fBconvert\fR, \fBtell me\fR, \fBgive me\fR, \fBthe\fR, \fBa\fR, \fBof\fR

.SH SUPPORTED UNITS

.SS Length
\fBm\fR (meters), \fBkm\fR (kilometers), \fBcm\fR (centimeters), \fBmm\fR (millimeters), \fBum\fR (micrometers), \fBnm\fR (nanometers), \fBin\fR (inches), \fBft\fR (feet), \fByd\fR (yards), \fBmi\fR (miles), \fBly\fR (lightyears), \fBau\fR (astronomical units), \fBpc\fR (parsecs)

.SS Time
\fBs\fR (seconds), \fBms\fR (milliseconds), \fBus\fR (microseconds), \fBns\fR (nanoseconds), \fBmin\fR (minutes), \fBh\fR (hours), \fBd\fR (days), \fBwk\fR (weeks), \fByr\fR (years)

.SS Mass
\fBkg\fR (kilograms), \fBg\fR (grams), \fBmg\fR (milligrams), \fBug\fR (micrograms), \fBlb\fR (pounds), \fBoz\fR (ounces), \fBton\fR (tons)

.SS Data
\fBbit\fR, \fBB\fR (bytes), \fBKB\fR, \fBMB\fR, \fBGB\fR, \fBTB\fR, \fBPB\fR, \fBEB\fR, \fBZB\fR, \fBYB\fR

.SS Volume
\fBL\fR (liters), \fBmL\fR (milliliters), \fBgal\fR (gallons), \fBqt\fR (quarts), \fBpt\fR (pints), \fBcup\fR, \fBfloz\fR (fluid ounces), \fBtbsp\fR (tablespoons), \fBtsp\fR (teaspoons)

.SS Temperature
\fBC\fR (Celsius), \fBF\fR (Fahrenheit), \fBK\fR (Kelvin), \fBR\fR (Rankine) - use \fBtemp()\fR function

.SS Other Categories
Pressure: \fBPa\fR, \fBkPa\fR, \fBbar\fR, \fBatm\fR, \fBpsi\fR
.br
Energy: \fBJ\fR, \fBkJ\fR, \fBcal\fR, \fBkcal\fR, \fBWh\fR, \fBkWh\fR, \fBBTU\fR, \fBeV\fR
.br
Power: \fBW\fR, \fBkW\fR, \fBMW\fR, \fBGW\fR, \fBhp\fR
.br
Speed: \fBm/s\fR, \fBkm/h\fR, \fBmph\fR, \fBkn\fR (knots), \fBmach\fR
.br
Angles: \fBrad\fR, \fBdeg\fR

