.SH MATHEMATICAL CONSTANTS

\fBpi\fR (3.14159...), \fBe\fR (2.71828...), \fBtau\fR (6.28318...), \fBi\fR (imaginary unit), \fBinf\fR (infinity), \fBnan\fR (NaN)

.SH FUNCTIONS

.SS Trigonometric
\fBsin\fR, \fBcos\fR, \fBtan\fR, \fBasin\fR, \fBacos\fR, \fBatan\fR, \fBatan2\fR(y,x)
.PP
All trig functions handle complex arguments.

.SS Hyperbolic
\fBsinh\fR, \fBcosh\fR, \fBtanh\fR, \fBasinh\fR, \fBacosh\fR, \fBatanh\fR

.SS Logarithmic & Exponential
\fBlog\fR (natural log), \fBlog10\fR (base 10), \fBlog2\fR (base 2), \fBlog1p\fR (log(1+x)), \fBexp\fR, \fBexpm1\fR

.SS Roots & Powers
\fBsqrt\fR, \fBcbrt\fR, \fBpow\fR(x,y)

.SS Rounding & Absolute
\fBabs\fR, \fBfloor\fR, \fBceil\fR, \fBtrunc\fR, \fBround\fR(x,n), \fBsign\fR

.SS Factorial & Combinatorics
\fBfactorial\fR(n), \fBgcd\fR(a,b,...), \fBlcm\fR(a,b,...), \fBperm\fR(n,r), \fBcomb\fR(n,r), \fBnPr\fR, \fBnCr\fR

.SS Complex Numbers
\fBreal\fR(z), \fBimag\fR(z), \fBconj\fR(z), \fBphase\fR(z), \fBpolar\fR(z), \fBrect\fR(r,phi)

.SS Statistics
\fBmean\fR(x,...), \fBmedian\fR(x,...), \fBmode\fR(x,...), \fBstd\fR(x,...), \fBvariance\fR(x,...), \fBsum\fR(x,...), \fBmin\fR(x,...), \fBmax\fR(x,...)

.SS Prime Numbers
\fBisprime\fR(n), \fBprimefactors\fR(n), \fBnextprime\fR(n), \fBprevprime\fR(n)

.SS Random
\fBrandom\fR(), \fBrandint\fR(a,b), \fBrandrange\fR(a,b), \fBuniform\fR(a,b), \fBrandn\fR(), \fBgauss\fR(mu,sigma), \fBseed\fR(n)

.SS Bitwise
\fBbitand\fR(a,b), \fBbitor\fR(a,b), \fBbitxor\fR(a,b), \fBbitnot\fR(a), \fBbitlshift\fR(a,b), \fBbitrshift\fR(a,b), \fBbin\fR(n), \fBhex\fR(n), \fBoct\fR(n)

.SS Memory & Variables
\fBstore\fR(x), \fBrecall\fR(), \fBMR\fR (alias), \fBMplus\fR(x), \fBMminus\fR(x), \fBMC\fR (clear)
.br
\fBsetvar\fR(name,value), \fBgetvar\fR(name), \fBdelvar\fR(name), \fBlistvars\fR(), \fBclearvars\fR()

.SS Utility
\fBclamp\fR(x,lo,hi), \fBhypot\fR(x,y,...), \fBpercentof\fR(p,total), \fBaspercent\fR(x,total), \fBdegrees\fR(x), \fBradians\fR(x)

.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES

.PP
The CLI does not expose environment variable overrides for calculator input length or cache size. MCP mode reads \fBEGGCALC_MCP_PROFILE\fR and \fBEGGCALC_MCP_SCHEMA_DETAIL\fR.

.SH EXIT STATUS

.TP
0
Success - expression evaluated correctly.

.TP
1
Invalid expression - syntax error or unsupported operation.

.TP
2
Input too long - exceeded maximum input length.

.SH FILES

.TP
\fB~/.eggcalc_config.py\fR (or \fB./eggcalc_config.py\fR)
Optional user configuration file for custom constants and functions.
.PP
.nf
  # Example eggcalc_config.py
  CUSTOM_CONSTANTS = {
      "earth_radius": 6371,  # km
  }

  CUSTOM_FUNCTIONS = {
      "circle_area": lambda r: 3.14159 * r ** 2,
  }
.fi

.SH SECURITY

\fBcalc\fR uses AST-based parsing instead of \fBeval\fR(), providing:
.IP \(bu 2
No arbitrary code execution
.IP \(bu
Controlled function access (whitelist only)
.IP \(bu
No access to files, network, or system resources
.IP \(bu
Built-in DoS protection (max nesting, exponents, factorial size)

.PP
For untrusted input, use \fBevaluate_with_timeout()\fR from the Python API to prevent long-running calculations.

.SH PYTHON API

.PP
.nf
  from eggcalc import evaluate_raw, evaluate

  # Natural language and units (use this for user input)
  result = evaluate_raw("five plus three")    # 8
  result = evaluate_raw("30m + 100ft")        # 60.48 m

  # Pre-normalized expressions (faster, no spaces allowed)
  result = evaluate("5+3")                   # 8

  # With caching for repeated queries
  from eggcalc import evaluate_cached
  result = evaluate_cached("five plus three")

  # Thread-safe webapp wrapper
  from eggcalc import EggCalcApp
  app = EggCalcApp(cache_size=1000)
  result = app.calculate("five plus three")
.fi

